  "passage": "The elevator in Grandma's apartment building broke on Sunday. She lived on the fourth floor, so going outside became difficult.\nHer neighbors made a plan. One brought groceries. Another took out her trash. A teenager helped carry her laundry downstairs.\nThe repair took three days. When the elevator worked again, Grandma baked cookies and gave them to everyone who helped.\nA neighbor said, \"You do not need to thank us so much.\"\nGrandma answered, \"I am not only thanking you for carrying things. I am thanking you for remembering me.\"\nThe broken elevator was inconvenient, but it showed something good. People living in the same building were not just people behind doors. They could become a small community.",
